#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalzium; provides you with all kinds of information about the Periodic "
"Table of the Elements. You can lookup lots of information about the elements "
"and also use visualizations to show them. It is free and licensed under the "
"&GNU; Public License."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can visualize the Periodic Table of the Elements by groups, blocks, "
"acidic behavior, families, crystal structure or different states of matter. "
"You can plot data for a range of elements for properties like the density or "
"the atomic mass. You can go back in time and see what elements were known at "
"a given date. You can also calculate the molecular mass of molecules."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kalzium; quick start guide"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here is &kalzium; the first time you run it, either from the K menu-"
">Edutainment->Science->Kalzium or with <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;"
"<keycap>F2</keycap></keycombo> and entering <command>kalzium</command> into "
"the field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&kalzium; main window</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&kalzium; main window</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalzium; is divided in a sidebar on the left (in red, 1) and the table view "
"(in blue, 2) which shows the elements of the periodic table. The standard "
"menubar allows you to choose what you want to display and the status bar "
"reports facts. You can hide the sidebar using the <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Hide Sidebar</guimenuitem> </"
"menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you move the mouse cursor on an element of the table, a tooltip appears "
"with a picture of this element if available, its number and its mass. In the "
"sidebar is displayed an overview of the current element in the "
"<guilabel>Overview</guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can disable the tooltips using the <menuchoice> <guimenu>View</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Hide tooltip</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can choose several views for the table: display the elements per "
"families, per groups, per crystal structure, depending on their acidic "
"behaviour, &etc;. You can change all that in the menubar in the <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Look</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to know facts about a precise element, click on it in the table "
"and the information dialog will be displayed."
msgstr ""

