msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:572
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Overview</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:576
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Overview tab is the first one and it shows you an overview of the "
"element the mouse is over."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:580
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Calculate</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:582
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Calculate tab is the second in the sidebar. It alows you to calculate "
"molecules weights."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid "You are first presented with the following icons and text:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:590
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Calculate</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:592
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Calculate</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:596
#, no-c-format
msgid "You have to click on the elements that compose the molecule."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:603
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Weight</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:605
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Weight</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:609
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can remove some elements after you click on the Remove icon. You can "
"also clear all the elements with the Clear icon on the most right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:612
#, no-c-format
msgid "Timeline"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:614
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Timeline feature allows you to explore the elements of the set time "
"period. This is great for getting a feel for how the PSE evolved over time, "
"as more and more elements were discovered. If you move the slider you will "
"notice that some elements disappear if you move it to the left and reappear "
"if you move it to the right. Furthermore the number will change constantly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The number represents the date you are looking at. If you move the slider to "
"&eg; 1856 you will only see the elements which where known in the year 1856."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:627
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will notice that some elements are not even shown in the current year. "
"This is because some of the elements have not been discovered yet but are "
"predicted to exist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:639
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>Timeline</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:641
#, no-c-format
msgid "The PSE back in time (elements known in 1856)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:648
#, no-c-format
msgid "State of Matter"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:649
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the State of Matter function, you can choose a temperature and view the "
"state of each element at that temperature. You can easily visualize how many "
"elements and what elements are, for example, solid at a given temperature. "
"So you can learn that almost all are solid at very low temperatures and that "
"most are liquid or even vaporous at high temperatures."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:658
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>State of Matter</quote> Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:660
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalzium; can show you which elements are solid/liquid/vaporous at a given "
"temperature."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:667
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show/Hide Legend"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:668
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Show/Hide Legend action allows you to display the legend for the scheme "
"you are in (Groups, Blocks, Acid Behavior). The legend is displayed by "
"default but if you hide it, it will stay hidden until you choose to show it. "
"&kalzium; will keep this setting in its configuration file, so that the next "
"time you run it, the setting will be as you left it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:677
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &kalzium;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:679
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalzium; has many configuration options, which you can access by opening "
"the configuration dialog by selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure &kalzium;...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> "
"from the menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:685 index.docbook:699 index.docbook:715
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure &kalzium; Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:691
#, no-c-format
msgid "Colors"
msgstr "Colors"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:695
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Colors</guilabel> tab, you can change the different colors "
"for each scheme."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:705
#, no-c-format
msgid "Units"
msgstr "Unitats"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:709
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Units</guilabel> tab, you can choose the units. You can "
"select if you prefer kJ/mol by default or you can choose eV. The Temperature "
"is in Kelvin by default but you can change to degrees Celsius or degrees "
"Fahrenheit."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:721
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Miscellaneous</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:725
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Miscellaneous</guilabel> tab, you can find other options "
"not related with the previous tabs."
msgstr ""

